Package: LICmethods
Type: Package
Title: Protein Regulatory Networks of Mother-Daughter Cell Pairs from Live-Cell Imaging
Version: 0.13.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shirley", "Mathur", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "shirmath@uw.edu"),
    person("Kevin", "Lin", role = "aut", email = "kzlin@uw.edu")
  )
Description: Jointly estimates the ordinary-differential-equation regulatory
    networks of a mother yeast cell and one of her daughters from live-cell
    time-lapse trajectories (PRNODE). Each protein's rate equation is fit as a
    three-block group lasso on integrated polynomial bases: a scaffold shared by
    the two cells plus a deviation per cell, with per-cell intercept and slope
    profiled out and one common inverse-variance loss weight; the smoothing
    level and the penalty are chosen together by a known-variance BIC. Includes the simulators the
    method is tested on (a scaffold-plus-deviation network generator with every
    edge type, an exact linear-ODE solver, a dataset builder whose truth carries
    the pair's true inheritance), an inheritance measure (the one-frame flow-map similarity
    of the two fitted systems in standardized units at the tuned penalty) with its
    wrong-mother permutation test, edge-type scoring and plotting.
